.TH HOST 1
.SH NAME
host, nslookup \- the address of a name (DNS)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B host
.I name
.br
.B nslookup
.I name
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B host
asks the network server's DNS resolver for the IPv4 address of
.I name
and prints it
.RI ( name " has address " a.b.c.d ).
.B nslookup
does the same. Both are other names of
.BR fetch (1).
The DNS server is the one DHCP gave
.RB ( ifconfig (1)
shows it).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 if the name could not be resolved.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ping (1),
.BR ifconfig (1),
.BR fetch (1),
.BR netd (4)
.SH BUGS
IPv4 addresses only.
